---
// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
/**
 * Faq: eight questions as native <details>/<summary> (works without JS, keyboard accessible).
 * Answers are short and plain, from docs/content-inventory.md sections 2, 3, 5, 6, 10 and 11 (status as of product
 * origin/main e129848, 2026-11-26). Nothing here claims a feature exists that does not. No props.
 */
import '../../styles/area-s4.css';
import Icon from '../ui/Icon.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../../site';

const items = [
  {
    q: 'Is it ready?',
    a: 'No. Cutweave is pre-alpha, in Phase 2 of 7, and there is no download or installer yet. Phase 1 is done: on 25 November the project owner signed off M1, in which the editor and a scripted agent each imported clips, cut and exported a 1080p MP4, and the two files were byte-identical. That was checked on Windows only; macOS and Linux are deferred, not dropped. Phase 2, the core editor, is 26 of 82 work packages in. You can run the editor from source today, but speed changes, compound clips, an export queue and captions are not built. The roadmap shows what is built and what is left.',
    link: { href: '/roadmap/', label: 'See the roadmap' },
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need an account?',
    a: 'No. There is no account, no watermark and no feature tiers. The engine in the repo has no sign-in and opens no outbound connections, and a test checks that. Crash reports will be opt-in, and update checks can be turned off. These are written into the project principles.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can an agent use it today?',
    a: 'Yes in the repo, no in an app you can install. The engine serves MCP over HTTP and over stdio, with one execute tool that reaches all 115 commands and queries. An agent can import real media, cut, get a rendered frame as an image, undo and start an export. In the M1 test a scripted agent, with no window open, made the same cut as the editor and the two exports were byte-identical. A recorded session on the agent page shows an agent importing real clips, cutting, looking at a rendered frame and exporting. The tool set is still growing in Phase 2.',
    link: { href: '/agents/#real-run', label: 'Read a real run' },
  },
  {
    q: 'What do AI features cost?',
    a: 'You bring your own keys for the providers you choose and pay them directly. Every AI run shows an estimated price first, and you can set budget caps. The AI gateway is planned for Phase 5.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why GPL?',
    a: 'The core is GPL-3.0-or-later so it stays open for everyone who uses it. The plugin SDK is MIT or Apache-2.0, so plugin authors choose their own terms. A written plugin exception is a draft pending legal review.',
    link: { href: '/open-source/', label: 'Read about the license' },
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I build plugins?',
    a: 'Not yet. Plugins are planned for Phase 6, in layers from data packs and GPU effects to WASM components and UI panels. The built-in effects and providers use the same interfaces.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will it run on the web or mobile?',
    a: 'The first release is a desktop app. A browser version and a mobile companion are both on the list for after 1.0, and neither is promised.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who builds it?',
    a: 'Mostly AI coding agents, working from public work packages, under human review. Review capacity is the bottleneck, and the project says so. Contributions from people and from agents are welcome, with a DCO sign-off on every commit.',
    link: { href: LINKS.contributing, label: 'Read the contributing guide', external: true },
  },
];
---
<div class="faq">
  {items.map((it) => (
    <details class="item">
      <summary>
        <span class="q">{it.q}</span>
        <Icon name="arrow-right" size="lg" class="chev" />
      </summary>
      <div class="a">
        <p>{it.a}</p>
        {it.link && <p><a href={it.link.href} target={it.link.external ? '_blank' : undefined} rel={it.link.external ? 'noopener' : undefined}>{it.link.label}</a></p>}
      </div>
    </details>
  ))}
</div>

<style>
  .faq { max-width: var(--content-narrow); border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--border-default); }
  .item { border-bottom: var(--border-thin) solid var(--border-default); }
  summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    min-height: var(--hit-touch);
    padding-block: var(--space-4);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
  }
  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  summary:hover .q { color: var(--text-primary); }
  summary:focus-visible { outline: var(--border-thick) solid var(--focus-ring); outline-offset: var(--border-thick); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
  .q { font-size: 18px; line-height: 26px; font-weight: 600; }
  .item :global(.chev) { color: var(--text-secondary); transition: transform var(--duration-base) var(--easing-standard); }
  .item[open] :global(.chev) { transform: rotate(90deg); }
  .a { padding-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: var(--prose-max); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-2); color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: var(--text-body-size); line-height: var(--text-body-line); }
  .a a { color: var(--text-primary); text-underline-offset: var(--space-0-5); }
</style>
